---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy & analytics — Robotail Journal" description="Choose whether to allow optional audience measurement on Robotail Journal." noindex={true}>
  <article class="wrap analytics-settings">
    <h1>Privacy &amp; analytics</h1>
    <p>Robotail Journal uses Vercel Web Analytics to count page views without analytics cookies or advertising tags. Reading a story does not require a consent click. Our previous Google Analytics tag is no longer loaded.</p>
    <p>Vercel aggregates page, referrer, device and approximate location information. It uses a short-lived request hash to estimate visitors; this is not a verified count of people. We remove query strings and fragments from the page URL before sending a page view.</p>
    <p><a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Vercel handles analytics data</a></p>
    <p data-analytics-status aria-live="polite">Checking this browser’s page-count settings.</p>
    <div class="analytics-actions"><button type="button" data-analytics-allow>Enable cookieless page counts</button><button type="button" data-analytics-decline>Stop page counting</button></div>
    <h2>Exclude your own visits</h2>
    <p>If you manage this journal, exclude this browser before reviewing pages. This affects only this browser on this site. Use the same setting separately on your other browsers and devices; it cannot remove past visits.</p>
    <div class="analytics-actions"><button type="button" data-analytics-exclude>Exclude this browser</button><button type="button" data-analytics-include>Remove browser exclusion</button></div>
    <p>You can change these preferences here at any time. Only the opt-out and owner-exclusion preferences are saved in this browser; they are not visitor identifiers. We also respect existing explicit opt-outs, Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
